course: dictionary
lesson: 8164
title: Resettle: a new place to settle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To resettle means to move people to a new place to live, often after war, disaster or danger. It can also mean to settle down or get comfortable again. The word has two parts: re- means again, and settle means to make a home or become calm, so resettle means to settle again.
explain: Look at the context. «It was reported that Australia has for many years turned back boats and sent people arriving by boat to centres in other countries, called offshore processing, while also resettling some refugees each year.» The clues are refugees and centres, which tell you people have fled danger and need a new home. So resettling means helping them move and live somewhere new.
explain: The word can also be everyday. A baby may take a while to resettle after waking up, which means calming down and getting comfortable again. Always ask: are people moving to a new home, or is someone becoming calm again?
fact: Resettle means to move people to a new place to live, often after war, disaster or danger.
fact: Refugees are people who have had to leave their country because they were not safe there.
fact: Resettle can also mean to settle down or get comfortable again, like a baby after waking up.
fact: The re- at the start means again, so resettle means to settle again.
fact: «Resettle into» and «resettled in» show where someone moves to live, such as a family resettled in a new town.
exercise: «Australia has been resettling some refugees each year.» What does resettling mean here? | *To move people to a new place to live | To count money in a shop | To break something into small pieces | To sing loudly at a school show
exercise: The baby took a long time to resettle after the loud noise woke her. What does resettle mean? | *To calm down and get comfortable again | To shout for a long time | To cry until the house is empty | To go to sleep forever
exercise: What does the re- in resettle mean? | Not | Before | *Again | Very
test: «Families were resettled in new homes after the flood.» What does resettled mean? | Washed away by the river | *Moved to a new home to live | Built a bridge over the river | Went fishing for the day
test: Which phrase means helping people who had to flee danger to start a new life somewhere safe? | *resettle refugees | paint the walls | count the sheep | cook a family dinner
exam: «The kitten took an hour to resettle on her blanket.» What does resettle mean? | To buy a bigger bed | *To get comfortable again | To run away from the house | To paint the blanket a new colour
